# platform.rp2350_touch_lcd_28.audio

The Waveshare RP2350-Touch-LCD-2.8's Speaker and Microphone. The board's
schematic shows a TI PCM5101A DAC feeding an APA2068 amplifier, and no
microphone.

The Speaker is an mm.audio Out straight over mm.mcu I2S, because the PCM5101A
has no control port: its straps select I2S framing and leave it unmuted, its
system-clock pin is grounded, and the amplifier's mute is tied off and its
shutdown pulled up. Nothing in software enables, mutes, or configures either
part; the program controls only the stream. The link is bit clock GP2, word
clock GP3, and data GP4, with sixteen-bit slots.

With SCK grounded the DAC generates its clocks from the bit clock with its
PLL. The datasheet's table of rates that PLL accepts with a bit clock of 32
times the rate is 32, 44.1, 48, 96, 192, and 384 kHz; the Speaker configures
the nearest of the first five, and a caller asking for another gets that one
back as its actual Format. The DAC holds its outputs at zero while it
resynchronises, so the Speaker configures the link at configure and keeps its
clocks running until the provider is gone: starting and stopping playback
changes only what the transmitter sends, not whether the DAC is locked.

It keeps the Out contract as mm.audio.es8311's Output does: service offers its
pending run first and reads the Stream only when nothing is pending, each
mono sample goes to both slots, transmitter silence is reported as underrun,
and position and pending come from the transmitter's progress.

The Microphone answers Unsupported to every call: there is none, and the ADC
pins that could take one, GP26 and GP27, are the battery enable and sense.

None of this is qualified on hardware.
